# Conformance probe pack for the `cbor` wire (spec 0.28): constants of the
# three types, and kinds chosen by a `when` on text, on a bool, on a two-step
# path, on an integer above 2^63-1, and by `when ... present`. One kind writes
# a `when` value at a path a `field` also names, and a common `const` stands
# at a path a common `field` names. A `const` beyond 2^64-1 is text (ruling
# 19), and a group with a `.` body reads scalar elements (ruling 14). No
# line's path but a `when ... present` is a proper prefix of another's in
# one scope (ruling 13).
format        conformance-cbor-kinds
version       0.28.0
distribution  public
source        "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses          probe
wire          cbor

field    uid        1     text
field    probe.y    v     int
const    v          -0007
const    s          =12
const    ok         true
const    t          18446744073709551616
group    probe.nums 9
  field  probe.val  .     int
end

# chosen on encode when lat is present; the fields walk into 7 (ruling 13
# lets a `when ... present` name a prefix of another line's path)
kind     located
when     7          present
requires lat
field    lat        7.1   float
field    lon        7.2   float

# the when value is written over the field at m
kind     overlay
when     m          fixed
requires probe.s1
field    probe.s1   m     text

# a when on a two-step path
kind     deep
when     3.1        5
requires probe.val
field    probe.val  3.2   uint

# an integer when above 2^63-1
kind     big
when     0          18446744073709551615
requires probe.x
field    probe.x    4     int

# when ... present on an item no other line walks into: residue whole
kind     marked
when     8          present
requires probe.n
field    probe.n    2     int

# a text when; the first kind with no requires, so the encode default
kind     text
when     k          track
field    probe.n    2     int

# a bool when
kind     flagged
when     b          true
field    probe.n    2     int
